# NetClaw Mobile — release signing template.
#
# Copy to `key.properties` (same directory) and fill in real values. That file
# is gitignored, as are *.jks and *.keystore — none of it may ever be committed.
#
# If `key.properties` is ABSENT the build still succeeds, but signs the release
# with the Android DEBUG key and prints a warning. Such an APK is fine for
# sideloading (see SIDELOAD.md) and impossible to upload to Play.
#
# Generate an upload keystore:
#
#   keytool -genkey -v -keystore ~/netclaw-upload-keystore.jks \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias upload
#
# LOSING THIS KEYSTORE IS UNRECOVERABLE. Once a listing is published with it,
# there is no way to ship an update without it — only a brand-new listing with
# zero installs. Back it up in two places off this machine before first upload,
# and enrol in Play App Signing. See PLAY-STORE-ROADMAP.md phase 2.

storeFile=/absolute/path/to/netclaw-upload-keystore.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=upload
keyPassword=
